## Versioning

4-digit format: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH.MICRO`. Source of truth: `VERSION` file. Status: `docs/PROGRESS.md`. Backlog: `docs/TODOS.md`.

## Product scope

When `docs/SPEC.md` exists with an `## Authority` section, read it before
planning, roadmap, review and release decisions. Its selected target, intended users, audience ceiling, accepted
limitations and release policy override generic scope and version-bump
defaults. A backlog entry or review label alone does not create a release
requirement. Preserve approved scope; defer unrelated improvements with a
revisit trigger. `/project-spec` establishes these decisions and any transition
from the initial version format. Open a current supporting document only when
its listed role bears on the decision; superseded plans/specs are historical
only. Do not load them routinely or extract new backlog items from them.

